# Cosora Admin Panel — Feature Audit

Date: 2026-10-02
Scope: `Cosora-Admin` (`main` @ `5997705`) and `textile-spark-net` (`main` @ `66876b2`), same Supabase project (`vxdhhgdfubqedfpwfyrb`). This supersedes the 2026-09-27 findings doc in full — almost every gap logged there has since been closed. Read `documentation/claude.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` in both repos before touching either codebase; this audit draws heavily on both rather than re-deriving everything from scratch.

Everything below is either: (a) read from the current committed source and the live migration ledger, (b) taken from a changelog entry that documents its own verification, or (c) independently re-checked live this session (noted inline as "confirmed live" where it matters — a vendor-PII check and the semantic-matching check in particular contradicted the written docs and needed a direct test). Nothing here was exercised by clicking through the actual browser UI; there is still no admin login available to this session.

## How the two repos relate

`Cosora-Admin` is the admin panel (separate Vercel deployment). `textile-spark-net` is the buyer/vendor app. They share one Supabase project, and a change that affects both gets an entry in both changelogs. `textile-spark-net/documentation/claude.md` is the authoritative running memory for business rules and platform facts — read it first in any new session on this project, before the 600KB-plus `changelog.md`.

**Branches merged into `Cosora-Admin` main**, in order: admin-schema separation (Phase 5b/5c), FAQs, Admin Log + Manager role, manager-team-roles, cron-job removal, admin completion Phases 1–12 (role separation, vendor PII, payments ledger, customers, leads, live activity, site content, discounts, blog CMS, least-privilege reads, RLS performance), Help & Support P4 (admin console).

**Not yet merged to `Cosora-Admin` main** (live as a feature branch only): `admin-staff/registration`, `help-support/p5-content`, `help-support/p6-background`. The corresponding database migrations for all three (`admin_staff_registry`, `faqs_seller_help_and_translations`, `help_content_p5`, `registration_documents`, `plan_changes_and_refund_guarantee`, `help_content_documents_plans`) are already applied live, 2026-10-02 — so the schema and RPCs exist in the database today with **no admin UI yet pointed at them**. Don't assume "the migration is live" means "the panel can act on it."

## Database shape at a glance

- `public` — the buyer/vendor app's tables (products, rfqs, quotes, conversations, messages, advertisements, subscriptions, vendor_profiles/buyer_profiles, blog tables, site_banners/site_theme, discount_codes, csp_violation_reports, etc).
- `admin` — walled off from `public`, reachable only through RPCs: `admin_users`, `audit_log`, `account_suspensions`, `conversation_reviews`, `chat_block_reasons`, `keyword_blocklist`, `flag_patterns`, `ad_review_log`, `ad_reason_codes`, `admin_flags`, `engagement_event_failures`, `vendor_contact_reveals`, `customer_summary_meta`, `customer_tags`, `profile_tags`, `discount_codes`/`discount_redemptions`/`discount_attempts`, `payment_entries`, `lead_rows` (a view), `staff_members` (schema live, no reader yet — see Admin Staff below).
- `support` — new schema for the Help & Support feature (three migrations, `support_schema`/`support_requester_rpcs`/`support_admin_rpcs`), applied and deployed, rollout flag currently **Off**.
- 251 migrations total on the live ledger, 112 of them dated 2026-09-27 or later. This project moves fast; re-check `list_migrations` at the start of any new session rather than trusting a prior audit's row counts.

