## Feature-by-feature

### Products — moderation queue
**Status: working.** Three tabs by status (under review / live / rejected). Approve/reject writes `products.status` + `rejection_reason` directly; `trg_products_moderation` (BEFORE trigger) enforces `product_moderator`/`super_admin` only, and — since admin completion Phase 1 (2026-09-27) — a rejection without a reason is now refused **in the database**, not just the UI textarea. Confirmed in the migration ledger (`20260927150304_moderation_and_campaign_guards`).

### Video Closeups — moderation queue
**Status: working.** Mirrors Products on `product_videos`. The old vendor-wide bulk-approve RPC (which silently also approved that vendor's pending products and catalogues) was replaced in Phase 3 (2026-09-27) with `approve_vendor_videos_bulk()`, scoped to videos only, returning the actual count moved.

### Ads — review queue + legacy screen + monitoring
**Status: working, bypass closed.** The 2026-09-27 finding (an `ads_moderator`/`super_admin` could `UPDATE advertisements SET status='active'` directly, skipping the review RPCs and the `admin.ad_review_log` entirely) is fixed: `admin_rpc_guards` and `moderation_and_campaign_guards` (both `20260927150...`) close the direct-write path — admins now change a campaign only through the review RPCs, confirmed by `documentation/claude.md`'s own rule: *"Admins change a campaign only through the review RPCs. `advertisements` has no admin write arm... Nobody deletes a reviewed campaign through the API, admins included."* The two ad-reason-code vocabularies (legacy free text vs. the fixed 8-code list) were unified in Phase 3: both screens now read `admin_ad_reason_codes()` from one table, `admin.ad_reason_codes`, and Phase 3's `after_panel_deploy_drop_bulk_and_enforce_reason_codes` migration makes a reason **mandatory** at the database level, not just in the form.

### Chat Review, Keywords, Patterns, Reasons
**Status: working.** `ChatReview.tsx`'s block flow is now one RPC call (`block_account_from_review()`), replacing the old two-call sequence that could leave a user suspended with their triggering review still stuck "pending" — that specific race is gone. The 2026-09-27 finding that `admin_flag_pattern_add('.*', ...)` would be silently accepted and lock every chat on the platform is fixed: a chat flag pattern that matches ordinary messages is now refused with a reason, shown verbatim in `ChatPatterns.tsx`.

### Vendors + Vendor Detail
**Status: working.** KYC review (`set_vendor_document_verified`) unchanged: support/super_admin only, rejection reason mandatory in the database. **Vendor PII is now genuinely private** — this was the single highest-severity finding from 2026-09-27 (anon and authenticated could read every vendor's PAN, owner email, phone, address straight off `vendor_profiles`). Fixed 2026-09-27/28: eight columns (`pan`, `owner_email`, `phone`, `whatsapp`, `address_line`, `area`, `landmark`, `postal_code`) are revoked from client access and read only through `admin_vendor_private()` (super_admin, vendor_ops, support, finance_admin) on the admin side, and `my_vendor_private()` / `call_vendor_contact()` on the buyer/vendor side. **Confirmed live this session**, not just from the changelog: `information_schema.column_privileges` still lists stale-looking grant rows for `authenticated` on these columns (an artifact of Supabase registering grants from both the `postgres` and `supabase_admin` grantors — the same quirk `documentation/claude.md` documents for function EXECUTE grants), but an actual impersonated `SELECT pan, owner_email, phone, whatsapp, address_line FROM vendor_profiles` as `authenticated` returns **"permission denied for table vendor_profiles."** The real enforcement holds; only the informational catalog view looks out of date. Worth remembering: don't trust `information_schema` alone on this project for a privacy check — always confirm with a live impersonated read.

### Accounts (suspension)
**Status: working**, same behaviour as before: new-content creation blocked on suspension, existing live content untouched, KYC/reason requirements vary by RPC. No change logged here since 2026-09-27.

### Subscriptions & billing
**Status: working, now with reasons.** Plan change and cancel go through `admin_subscription_change_plan()` / `admin_subscription_cancel()`, both requiring a reason that's recorded into the Admin Log (`cosora.audit_reason` → `admin.audit_log.reason`). The direct `vendor_subscriptions` UPDATE this panel used to make is gone. The 2026-09-27 finding that **every** admin role (not just finance_admin/super_admin) could reprice or delete any `subscription_plans` row via direct table access is fixed: that write policy's admin arm now names `super_admin, finance_admin` specifically (`admin_write_role_separation`, `20260927145549`).

### Certificates
**Status: working.** `certificate_dispatch()` now checks the caller's role before its business-rule checks (Phase 1, 2026-09-27) — the 2026-09-27 finding that an unauthorized caller learned an operational fact (no delivery address on file) before being told they lacked permission is resolved by that reordering.

### Payments — real ledger (admin completion Phase 5)
**Status: working, real data.** The dev-seed fixture is gone. `admin.payment_entries` is a unified ledger (subscription payments, refunds as negative rows, unfinished checkouts, ad and certificate orders), read through `admin_payments_ledger()` / `admin_payments_summary()`, all amounts normalised to paise. Filtering, search and keyset paging run server-side. Rows with no Razorpay payment id (demo-mode activations) are totalled separately and flagged, matching Reports' convention. This closes the old "all revenue is simulated and the UI doesn't say so" gap — it now says so, on every affected row.

### Customers — real segments (admin completion Phase 6)
**Status: working, real data.** `admin.customer_summary` (materialized view, refreshed on page open at most once every 10 minutes — deliberately not a scheduled job) backs one row per customer account, with segment chips computed server-side. Super_admin and support can tag customers; tags are logged to the Admin Log. Cosora staff accounts are excluded from the customer list.

### Leads — the RFQ pipeline (admin completion Phase 7)
**Status: working, read-only.** New `/leads` page. See the dedicated write-up in the chat response for the full mechanism; in short, it reads `admin.lead_rows` (a view over `rfqs` + `quotes`) through `admin_leads_list()`, `admin_leads_summary()`, `admin_lead_detail()`. Six stages (new / unanswered / overdue / quoted / won / closed), an audience filter (open marketplace vs. direct-to-one-vendor), and timing figures (median time to first quote, % answered within 24h). Readable by super_admin, vendor_ops, product_moderator, support; writable by nobody — it's a reporting surface, not a moderation one. **Confirmed live**: 4 real RFQs exist today, 3 in "quoted" stage, 1 "unanswered" and already flagged "overdue" (the view's own threshold: active, zero quotes, more than 48 hours old).

### Live Activity (admin completion Phase 8)
**Status: working, real data.** No longer just a Clarity link. `admin_live_activity()` now reports real-time and windowed visitor counts, an hourly events chart, top products/sellers, and searches with at least 3 distinct searchers (same privacy floor as the vendor-facing buyer-geography feature). Clarity links still show when `VITE_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID` is configured.

### Site Content (admin completion Phase 9)
**Status: working, real data.** Dev-seed fixture gone. Vendor-dashboard banners (add/edit/reorder/schedule/on-off/delete) and site theme (5 colours + 2 fonts, contrast-checked against WCAG floors before Save is allowed) are both real, backed by `public.site_banners` / `public.site_theme` and the `admin_site_*` RPCs, propagated to the buyer app via a CDN snapshot (`site-config-snapshot` edge function). Banners are vendor-dashboard only — Mitra's explicit call, none on the buyer side.

### Discounts (admin completion Phase 10)
**Status: working, real data.** Dev-seed fixture gone. Codes apply to a plan, an ad campaign, or the Verified Certificate line, via `admin_discount_*` RPCs on `admin.discount_codes` / `admin.discount_redemptions`. Once a code has a confirmed use, its text/discount/target lock — you make a new code rather than edit a used one. The discount amount is always computed server-side (`discount-quote` edge function + `discount_check`/`discount_reserve` in the database); the browser only ever sends the code string.

### Blog / Cosora Journal (admin completion Phase 10)
**Status: new, working.** Not in the 2026-09-27 audit at all — built 2026-09-29/30. Three tabs (Articles, Categories, Landing page) write through `admin_blog_*` RPCs to a dedicated schema. Block-based article editor (text/heading/list/image/table/FAQ/quote/CTA/divider), full SEO fields with live title/description previews against the blog's real rendering rules (including the trailing " · The Cosora Journal" suffix, which an earlier version of the character counter forgot to account for), author picked from a real `public.authors` table rather than free text. Gated to super_admin only.

### FAQs / Quick Guides
**Status: working.** Unchanged mechanism (support + super_admin write via `admin_faq_*` RPCs, changes propagate to a CDN snapshot within about a minute). Quick Guides (Hindi/English/Gujarati) were added as part of the Support rollout (see below) and live under the same `/faqs` page.

### Support (new, admin completion / Help & Support P4)
**Status: built and deployed, rollout Off.** A full Support section: Inbox with view filters (waiting on us / open / mine / unassigned / resolved / closed / all), Callbacks, Fraud reports, App feedback, Support settings. Ticket view handles photos/audio/PDFs, masked phone reveals (logged to the Admin Log), take/assign/resolve/reopen/close with a reason. This is merged into `Cosora-Admin` main and the three underlying migrations are applied — **but the rollout flag is Off**, so the public-facing inbox receives nothing from real users yet. Manager role is read-only here by design (Andy's decision D-08); only super_admin and support act on tickets.

### Admin Staff Registration
**Status: schema-only, not in production.** `admin.staff_members` exists live (0 rows) with a comment confirming intent — "Staff registered from Cosora-Admin (admin-staff edge function): employee ID, work email, personal contact, temporary-password state" — but the UI branch (`admin-staff/registration`) is not merged into `Cosora-Admin` main. Don't report this as a working feature; it's mid-build.

### Admins + Admin Log
**Status: working**, unchanged since 2026-09-27: manager role can add/change/remove teammates in the five team roles only, last-super-admin protection confirmed, every admin write is append-only logged.

### Geography, Reports, System Health
**Status: working**, no material change logged since 2026-09-27 beyond System Health gaining a "Scheduled jobs" panel (see below) and a staleness warning on the embedding-health history.

### Scheduled jobs
All 12 Postgres cron jobs were deleted 2026-09-26 on Mitra's instruction, then the essential 7 were restored 2026-09-27 with a new 14-day history-prune job added: `account-deletion-sweep` + its alarm, `subscription-expiry-sweep`, `ads-schedule-sweep` (every 5 min), `faq-snapshots-refresh` (hourly), `embedding-health-log` (every 10 min), `fx-rates-refresh` (daily), `cron-history-prune`. **Deliberately still off:** `embedding-worker` and `vendor-catalog-recompute` (the two every-minute jobs — this matters for the Leads/lead-ranking discussion below), the embedding-health alarm, and two cache/rate-limit prune jobs. System Health's new "Scheduled jobs" panel (`admin_cron_status()`) shows every job's schedule, last run, 24h run/failure counts, and flags a job "overdue" if it's gone past twice its interval.

