## What's confirmed fixed since the 2026-09-27 audit

1. Vendor PAN/GSTIN/phone/email world-readable via `vendor_profiles` → **fixed**, confirmed live by impersonated read.
2. Every admin role (not just the intended ones) could reprice/delete subscription plans, write `quotes`, bulk-approve across tables, read all KYC/contracts/invoices regardless of role → **fixed**, database write/read policies now name their roles explicitly (admin completion Phases 1 and 11).
3. Ad review bypassable by direct `UPDATE advertisements` → **fixed**, no admin write arm exists on that table any more.
4. Product/video rejection reasons not enforced server-side → **fixed** for both.
5. Chat flag patterns with no breadth guard (`.*` could lock every conversation) → **fixed**, refused with a reason.
6. Chat-review block flow was two non-atomic RPC calls → **fixed**, now one call.
7. Scheduled jobs silently deleted with no visibility → **fixed**, essential jobs restored and a status panel added.
8. All four dev-seed stub pages (Content, Payments, Customers, Discounts) → **all four are now real**, plus two entirely new real features (Blog, Leads) that didn't exist in any form before.

## New things worth flagging, found this session

1. **The RFQ form's "7-day deadline" is fiction.** `PostRequirement.tsx` tells every buyer: *"Every quote has an automatic 7-day deadline. Once it's reached, you'll get an option to extend it."* There is no `deadline` or `expires_at` column on `rfqs` or `quotes`, no job that closes an RFQ after 7 days, and no "extend" mechanism anywhere in the code or the schema. This is exactly the category of claim the project's own documented principle forbids ("the app never claims to have verified something it cannot verify" / no fabricated signals) — it should either be built or the line should come out.
2. **Semantic lead-matching is wired but currently benefits nobody.** The infrastructure is real: 33 of 34 products, all 4 RFQs, and 6 of 11 vendor catalogues have real OpenAI embeddings (confirmed live), and `match_vendor_rfqs` will score real similarity when both sides exist. But the feature is gated on an **active paid plan**, and right now exactly **1 vendor** on the whole platform has an active plan — and that one vendor's catalogue is not among the 6 with an embedding (vendor-catalogue embedding depends on the `vendor_catalog_recompute` job, which is deliberately left off, per the cron list above). So today, every vendor who opens their lead pool — paid or not — sees the same plain chronological list; the ranking code path exists but has zero live vendors who actually trigger it. This is a real product gap, not a bug: once `vendor_catalog_recompute` runs (or a one-off backfill is done) for that one paid vendor, ranking turns on for them specifically.
3. **`information_schema.column_privileges` is not reliable evidence of access on this project.** The vendor-PII check above is the second time (after the function-EXECUTE case `documentation/claude.md` already documents) that Supabase's dual-grantor behavior makes the catalog view show privileges that an actual impersonated query refuses. Any future security check on this schema should confirm with a live `SET LOCAL ROLE` test, not a grants query alone.

## Suggested next steps

1. Fix or remove the fake 7-day deadline claim in `PostRequirement.tsx` — cheapest possible fix, and it's a trust-eroding claim sitting on the buyer's primary conversion screen.
2. Decide whether to run `vendor_catalog_recompute` as a one-off for the single paid vendor (cheap, proves the ranking path end to end) versus turning the job back on generally (an ongoing OpenAI cost decision Mitra should make explicitly, not something to flip quietly).
3. Admin Staff Registration and Help-Support P5/P6 are mid-build on branches — worth explicitly deciding their priority rather than letting live, unused schema accumulate.
4. Support's rollout flag is the one lever standing between the built Support section and real traffic — flip it only once the "dummy OTP sign-in" bypass is retired (both are flagged in `textile-spark-net/documentation/securityflags.md`), since Help & Support's own launch checklist names that as a blocker.
